# What must never be committed, then what is merely regenerated.
#
# Ordered that way on purpose: the first section is a security boundary and the
# rest is housekeeping. A rule that moves out of the first section should be a
# deliberate decision, not a tidy-up.

# ---- secrets ---------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Every `.env` is ignored, and `.env.example` is un-ignored so the *names* of
# the settings can be committed without their values. That pairing matters here:
# the hub and both satellites refuse to start without PORTAL_PRINCIPAL_SECRET,
# so a newcomer needs to know it exists, and must not learn it from a leak.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
.npmrc.local

# Audit records carry principals, tenants and parameter digests.
# `PORTAL_AUDIT_LOG` is a path an operator chooses, and pointing it at the
# working tree during a local run must not put tenant data in a commit.
#
# One glob rather than the two it replaced, because those matched
# `portal.audit.jsonl` and `audit.jsonl` but not `portal-audit.jsonl` — which is
# the name `docker-compose.yml` itself uses. A rule whose coverage depends on
# which separator the operator typed is not a rule.
*audit.jsonl

# ---- dependencies ----------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
.pnpm-store/
.yarn/
jspm_packages/

# ---- build output ----------------------------------------------------------
dist/
build/
out/
*.tgz

# Next.js. `next-env.d.ts` is deliberately absent from this list: Next
# regenerates it, and its own documentation says to commit it.
.next/
.vercel/
next-env.d.ts.timestamp-*

# TypeScript incremental state. Project references write one per package.
*.tsbuildinfo
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

# ---- test and tooling caches -----------------------------------------------
coverage/
*.lcov
.nyc_output/
.vitest/
.turbo/
.cache/
.eslintcache
.stylelintcache

# Playwright. `test-results` and the reports are per-run artefacts; the browser
# download lives outside the repository.
test-results/
playwright-report/
blob-report/
playwright/.cache/
.playwright/
.last-run.json

# ---- .NET (sdk-csharp) -----------------------------------------------------
#
# Build output only. The generated sources are committed on purpose: they are
# what the drift check compares against, and what a consumer reads to see the
# surface without running a generator first.
#
# Scoped to the one package that produces them. A repo-wide `**/bin/` reads as
# housekeeping and is really a trap: `bin/` is an ordinary name for committed
# scripts, and the next person to add `scripts/bin/` would watch `git add`
# ignore it without saying why.
packages/sdk-csharp/**/bin/
packages/sdk-csharp/**/obj/

# ---- Python (satellite-fleet) ----------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# ---- logs and diagnostics --------------------------------------------------
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*
.node_repl_history
*.heapsnapshot
report.*.json

# ---- editors and OS --------------------------------------------------------
#
# `.vscode` is ignored except `extensions.json`, which is a shared statement
# about what this repository needs rather than anyone's personal settings.
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
